{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. Thank you all for being ready. Let's work through this systematically. As you know, a government export-control order has interrupted shipments of a key component, and several counterparties have already asked for our contractual position. We have a force-majeure provision in our principal supply agreement, but we have not yet sent an external notice under that provision. We can continue some production using existing inventory, but output will be materially below normal levels. Before we send any contractual disruption notice, I want each function to report its findings and recommended action. Here's the agenda: First, Thomas, please share your findings on the force-majeure notice requirements under the executed amendment and its notice exhibit. Second, Mei, please walk us through the operations picture — facility impact and production capacity. Third, Samuel, please share your time-sensitive insurance finding and how it bears on our notice timeline. Fourth, Nora, please share the customer-priority considerations from your discussions with our largest hospital-equipment customer. After we've heard from everyone, we'll synthesize and decide on next steps. Thomas, you're up first — please go ahead."}
```

